Nepali, Korean and Japanese languages have many phenomimes and psychomimes.

* [http://notesfromtheemeraldvalley.blogspot.jp/2011/02/to-kill-fish.html|Examples in Nepali]
* [http://raggedsign.blogs.com/caveatdumptruck/2011/01/caveat-phenomimes-and-psychomimes.html|Examples in Korean]
* Examples in Japanese are found in mangas.

In Lojban, the expressions parallel to them are accomplished with the ((Experimental cmavo|experimental cmavo)) ((tai'i)) and ((ci'oi)).